## 7. Explicitly deferred — acknowledged, not modeled

### [CXC-MODE-NAV-DEFERRED] What this design session raised that this spec deliberately does NOT model

- definition: the design session surfaced several statements beyond the `selection` archetype and the mode-nav fold. Per this task's explicit scope instruction, they are acknowledged HERE — so nothing below reads as silently dropped — and modeled NOWHERE in this document.
- the-control-display-taxonomy-is-confirmed-real: (audit round 1, C2 — strengthened, not hypothetical) David: *"the way we are using radio_button_group is functionally duplicative of a tab group, and we may well in the future need to have a different control that actually functions as a set of buttons or interactive elements responding to semantic messages."* (design session, 2026-08-18) named a genuinely DIFFERENT future control; this spec's [CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTOR-SKIN] correction uses only the first half of that sentence (the tab/radio duplication) and this line makes the LINK explicit rather than silently absorbing the second half into "settled." Audit round 1, C2, confirms the future need is REAL, not hypothetical, and grounds it concretely: *"The pcb in ~/maker/pcb/button_matrix_4x4 is a good physical example of what we want to be able to do with virtual buttons. The Galactica software object (compose-bus resident) will maintain state about all of its subsystems. The state of these subsystems will be published. Different button groups will react in different ways to different semantic messages. When the FTL engine is ready, a big red button labeled 'JUMP READY' may start to blink on screen and in real life (different subscribers)."* This is the `action`/`toggle`/`indicator` region of the full control/display taxonomy (`selection` / `value` / `action` / `toggle` / `indicator` / `output` / `custom`) this spec's scope explicitly excludes — not modeled here, but no longer a hypothetical placeholder: it is CONFIRMED future work with a named physical reference (`~/maker/pcb/button_matrix_4x4`) and a named worked scenario (JUMP READY, differently-reacting button groups, on-screen and real-world subscribers of the SAME published state).
- the-value-archetype-timer-keypad: "I will do something similar on the timer screen, I'll use a physical keypad to set the countown timer to, say 33 minutes instead of creating touch interfaces." (design session, 2026-08-18) — this describes SETTING a value (a duration), a different control archetype (`value`, not `selection`) from the full taxonomy this spec's scope explicitly excludes. Not modeled; parked for the follow-on session that specs the full taxonomy.
- the-semantic-ship-model: "yes, we will will have in the real world props momentary action buttons, actual toggle switches on/off state, illuminated buttons, thermal printers and even completely custom props like the thrust controller. Not all of these will have an on-screen doppelganger, but they will be mapped to a much more complex semantic model of the Galactica itself that can degade with damage, run low on fuel, run out of ammo, jump, be repaired and be resupplied." (design session, 2026-08-18) — explicitly excluded by this task's scope. Not modeled here at all.
- the-fingerprint-sensor-aside: "This is what lead me to realize that having a fingerprint sensor would add some interesting gameplay mechanics." (design session, 2026-08-18) — a gameplay idea sparked by the station/role discussion ([CXC-MODE-NAV-STATION-SCOPE]), not part of the settled mode-nav design. Not modeled; parked as a future idea, not a requirement of this spec.
- physical-hookup-not-spec-d-here: the 7-position rotary switches, the timer keypad, the `button_matrix_4x4` PCB, and any future fingerprint sensor are physical peripherals; their wiring is a SEPARATE maker-project slice, pattern-referenced the same way [CXC-CIC-ROTARY-HOOKUP] already treats the existing console/sub-tab rotaries — this spec only requires that whatever hardware realizes a selection publish the same namespace a soft selector would ([CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTION]).
- see-also: [CXC-CIC-ROTARY-HOOKUP], [CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTION]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MODE-NAV]

