## 8. Acceptance — machine signal + glass gate per surface

### [CXC-MODE-NAV-VERIFY] Acceptance — machine signal and glass gate per surface

- definition: each requirement carries a machine signal AND, for a human-perceptible surface, an explicit glass gate ([CXC-MENU-VERIFY] precedent). MODE-NAV-C1 through MODE-NAV-C5 test the GENERIC primitive/tree shape with neutral fixtures; MODE-NAV-C6 through MODE-NAV-C8 test the BSG instance specifically.

| ID | Requirement | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|----|-------------|-----------------|------------------------|
| MODE-NAV-C1 | A selection publishes the same `{index, key}` shape to the same namespace regardless of which realization (soft widget, physical control, Intelligence) issued it ([CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTION]) | a fixture publishes the identical payload from two simulated sources and asserts the subscriber-observed state is byte-identical | on glass: toggling CHRONO's nav via the touch selector and via a simulated rotary publish shows the identical active option |
| MODE-NAV-C2 | A soft selector's displayed active state is DERIVED from the published namespace value, never a local toggle ([CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTION], confirmed Q2) | a test publishes a selection change from a source OTHER than the widget under test and asserts the widget's rendered active state updates | on glass: an out-of-band publish (e.g. from an Intelligence) moves the on-screen selector without the screen being touched |
| MODE-NAV-C3 | A choice point in the tree is expressed by `children`, never a new [CXC-MENU-KINDS] token ([CXC-MODE-NAV-UNIFORM-LEAF]) | a lint pass over the mode-nav tree fixture asserts no node other than the 3 registered [CXC-MENU-KINDS] tokens appears anywhere in the tree's `annotation.kind` fields | n/a (structural) |
| MODE-NAV-C4 | A mode-nav selector is an EXTENDED [CXC-CIC-TABROW] instance, never a new widget class ([CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTOR-SKIN]) | a code-inspection test asserts every mode-nav selector instance is constructed from the same `TabWidget`/`ConsoleTabWidget` lineage [CXC-CIC-TABROW] documents, with no sibling "selector" class introduced | n/a (structural) |
| MODE-NAV-C5 | The resolver never reads a selection namespace, and a selection namespace never carries an asset path ([CXC-MODE-NAV-RESOLVER-SEAM]) | a property test asserts `resolve()`'s signature and return value are unaffected by any published selection state, and that no selection payload fixture contains a `bus://` value | n/a (structural) |
| MODE-NAV-C6 | STD's leaves resolve to byte-identical paths after the mode fold ([CXC-MODE-NAV-CIC-INSTANCE]) | a snapshot test asserts every one of the 35 STD (console, sub-tab) derived paths under the new 4-mode tree equals its pre-fold path from [CXC-MENU-CIC-INVENTORY] | n/a (structural) |
| MODE-NAV-C7 | DRADIS and EXT — prior-built, already running on (a private host name, not published) — resolve via their `annotation.path` override, never via directory-join ([CXC-MODE-NAV-CIC-INSTANCE]) | a fixture asserts `resolve(DRADIS)` returns the override path exactly and that removing the override makes [CXC-MENU-PATH]'s derivation produce a DIFFERENT (wrong) path, proving the override is load-bearing | on glass: DRADIS and EXT continue showing their existing, already-built mode surface under the new tree, unchanged from (a private host name, not published)'s current behavior |
| MODE-NAV-C8 | CHRONO's 3 options (SHIP TIME / JUMP COUNT / TIMER) resolve to 3 distinct leaves sharing the same art by default, with no baked-in per-option buttons — a done state, not a pending one ([CXC-MODE-NAV-CIC-CHRONO-INSTANCE]) | a snapshot test asserts `resolve(CHRONO > ship-time/jump-count/timer)` returns 3 distinct `bus://` paths; a screen-content test asserts no `slot:button@{ship-time,jump-count,timer}` element exists in any CHRONO leaf's SVG (regression coverage for art David has already cleaned up) | on glass: switching CHRONO's nav selector cycles the `colonial_clock` screen between its 3 states with no on-screen duplicate button row |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MODE-NAV]

