## 9. Design Decisions

### [DD-MODE-NAV-NAMESPACE-CONVENTION] DECIDED — `/`-delimited, matching [CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION] exactly, no dual support

- decision: whether the mode-nav tier's selection namespaces ([CXC-MODE-NAV-STATION-SCOPE]) use the EXISTING ratified [CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION] convention (`colonial_console/<station>/<level>`, `/`-delimited) or David's illustrative `station_n::colonial_ux::tab_1_selected` shape (`::`-delimited, root `colonial_ux`).
- chosen: `/`-delimited, the EXISTING [CXC-CIC-DUTY-STATION] convention. DECIDED — David ratified, audit round 1, Q4.
- rationale: David's own words settle both the visual-preference question (he finds `::` reads more like a namespace, `/` more like a file path) AND the practical one (not worth churning the existing convention or maintaining two). `mode` and `chrono` join `console`/`subtab`/`status`/`focus`/`identity`/`peripherals` as more `colonial_console/<station>/<level>` entries, zero impact on [CXC-CIC-TABROW]'s existing publishers.
- status: decided
- resolved-by: audit round 1, Q4, `docs/architecture/AUDIT-cic-mode-nav.md`
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MODE-NAV]

### [DD-MODE-NAV-SELECTOR-KIND-CONSOLIDATION] CLOSED — the existing art ([CXC-CIC-TABROW]) already resolves it; no widget-kind or grammar change needed

- decision: whether [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]'s registered `radio`/`tab_row` slot-grammar tokens should consolidate, given [CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTOR-SKIN]'s observation that they express one interaction model.
- chosen: CLOSED — no amendment to [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]'s registered set is needed, because the mode-nav tier's own selectors never touch that registry in the first place. [CXC-CIC-TABROW] already generalizes `row2`/`row3` as ONE widget with a style axis (`filled-background`/`pill-overlay`) — the CIC shell's own chrome-level tab rows, a DIFFERENT layer from a per-screen `slot:radio@…`/`slot:tab_row@…` composed binding. The mode row and CHRONO's nav are new instancings of [CXC-CIC-TABROW] at that SAME chrome layer, per [CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTOR-SKIN] — they never mint or bind a `slot:` label at all, so [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]'s registered tokens are simply not exercised by this spec.
- david-confirms-the-duplication-is-real: "the way we are using radio_button_group is functionally duplicative of a tab group" (design session, 2026-08-18) — correctly diagnosed the CONCEPTUAL duplication; [CXC-CIC-TABROW]'s pre-existing generalize-don't-fork treatment is what already resolves it in practice, one layer down from where [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]'s tokens live.
- residual-note: a NARROWER question — whether a per-screen composed SVG's own `slot:radio@…`/`slot:tab_row@…` bindings (a mechanism this spec's mode-nav tier does not use) should ALSO consolidate at the [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND] registry level — is real but genuinely OUT of this spec's scope; nothing here resolves or needs to resolve it, since no [CXC-MODE-NAV-*] node emits either token.
- invalidating_assumption: that no mode-nav selector will EVER need to be expressed as a per-screen `slot:` binding rather than CIC-shell chrome. If one does, this closure would need reopening against [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND] specifically.
- status: closed
- resolved-by: audit round 1 (coordinator instruction: "check whether the existing art already rules it; if so, close citing that") + [CXC-CIC-TABROW]'s pre-existing generalize-don't-fork precedent
- see-also: [CXC-CIC-TABROW], [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND], [CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTOR-SKIN]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MODE-NAV]

### [DD-MODE-NAV-RADIO-NAMESPACE-RENAME] OPEN — should [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]'s `radio` namespace segment rename to `mode`?

- decision: [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE] (itself still PROPOSED, not ratified) names its namespace segment `colonial_console/<station>/radio` — named after the WIDGET SHAPE (a radio row), the same naming-by-appearance tension [CXC-MODE-NAV-SELECTOR-SKIN] notes in [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]'s registry. This spec's [CXC-MODE-NAV-STATION-SCOPE] otherwise names namespace levels by SEMANTIC MEANING (`console`, `subtab`, `mode`, `chrono`) per [CXC-PS-GRANULARITY]'s "one namespace per meaning." Whether the mode row's namespace should rename `radio` -> `mode` for consistency is open. NOT ruled by David in audit round 1 — carried forward unchanged.
- alternatives: (a) rename `radio` -> `mode` as part of ratifying both [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE] and this spec together — CONSISTENT naming, but touches an already-drafted sibling spec's vocabulary; (b) leave `radio` as-is and treat it as a historical exception (the mode row predates this spec's naming discipline) — lowest churn, inconsistent naming persists.
- invalidating_assumption: that [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE] is still unbuilt at ratify time. If it has already shipped under `radio` before this fork is resolved, (a) becomes a migration, not a naming choice at design time.
- status: open
- see-also: [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MODE-NAV]

### [DD-MODE-NAV-CLOCK-WIDGET-REGISTRATION] OPEN — NEEDS-RENDER-ENGINEER-CONFIRM: does `colonial_clock` register as a [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND] interaction kind?

- decision: [CXC-MODE-NAV-CIC-CHRONO-INSTANCE] names each CHRONO leaf's clock slot `slot:colonial_clock@<binding>`. `colonial_clock` is DAVID-ORIGINATED (a rename of the prior 7-segment widget, requested and built earlier this session, already running on his glass — audit round 1, C4) but is NOT yet in [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]'s formally registered set (`button`, `radio`, `tab_row`, `text`, `readout`/`value`, `gauge`, `graph`, `table`, `led_bar`, …). Whether it registers as a genuinely new interaction kind, or is better named as a STYLE of an existing kind (e.g. a `readout` or `gauge` variant, per [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND]'s own "appearance is not a kind" rule), is unresolved. NOT ruled by David in audit round 1 — explicitly render-engineer territory, carried forward unchanged.
- needs-confirm: "⛔ NEEDS-RENDER-ENGINEER-CONFIRM. Unverified here: whether the ship-clock display (analog dial? digital readout? both, per mode?) is a genuinely distinct INTERACTION model from the existing registered kinds, or an appearance variant of `gauge`/`readout` that should not mint a new token at all — mirrors [CXC-MENU-SLOT-SIZING]'s own precedent of flagging an unregistered widget question rather than asserting an answer."
- alternatives: (a) register `colonial_clock` as a new interaction kind (Arm A, matching [DD-MENU-SLOT-SCENE-GRAMMAR]'s precedent of registering `scene` as a new kind rather than amending the grammar); (b) express it as a style parameter on an existing kind (`gauge` or `readout`), no new token.
- invalidating_assumption: that the clock's rendering genuinely differs in INTERACTION (not just appearance) from an existing kind. The widget itself is already built and live — this decision is about its REGISTRY status, not its existence.
- status: open
- see-also: [CXC-COMP-WIDGET-KIND], [CXC-MENU-SLOT-SIZING], [DD-MENU-SLOT-SCENE-GRAMMAR], [CXC-MODE-NAV-CIC-CHRONO-INSTANCE]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MODE-NAV]

